# pcre2 vulnerability in Alpine 3.19/3.24; pinned upstream official images we
# cannot rebuild until publishers ship new tags. The socket proxy only
# communicates over a local Unix socket and never parses untrusted regex;
# haproxy uses pcre2 only for its own static config patterns.
#
# Carriers:
#   - haproxy:2.8.28-alpine
#   - tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy:v0.5.0
# Reachability: input-path-unreachable
# Reachability evidence: pcre2 is never reached with untrusted input. The
# socket proxy never parses a regex from any source; haproxy compiles only the
# patterns written into config/haproxy.cfg, which is a bind-mounted static
# file and not attacker-reachable. haproxy is published on 443/80, so the
# exposure of this carrier is network-wide — the premise that holds is the
# input path, not the network path.
# Severity: HIGH
# Re-check when: the carrier images ship a rebuilt Alpine base with patched
# pcre2
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2027-01-05

# Out-of-bounds write in libbrotli1 1.1.0-2build2 (fixed in 1.1.0-2ubuntu0.1)
# in grafana 13.2.4-ubuntu base. Grafana is a third-party pinned image bound
# only to internal monitoring network (${AGENT_BIND_IP:-127.0.0.1}); it does
# not decompress untrusted brotli payloads. Pinned upstream image we cannot
# rebuild independently; the fix only reaches us when Grafana rebuilds on the
# updated Ubuntu 24.04 package.
#
# Carriers:
#   - grafana/grafana:13.2.4-ubuntu
# Reachability: internal-monitoring-only
# Severity: MEDIUM
# Re-check when: grafana/grafana publishes a tag rebuilt with libbrotli1 >=
# 1.1.0-2ubuntu0.1
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2027-01-25

# Go crypto/x509 can build a verified chain through an intermediate
# certificate the platform trust store no longer trusts (CVSS 6.8,
# AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R). Trivy reports it against the Go stdlib embedded in
# grafana 13.2.4-ubuntu (14 bundled binaries, Go <= 1.27.1) and alertmanager
# v0.34.1; the fix is a rebuild on Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3, which only the
# publisher can do. Both are the newest published tags in their release line
# (checked 2026-10-23), so no upgrade we can take clears it. Phase 847g bumped
# every sibling monitoring image that DID ship a fixed rebuild (loki 3.7.9,
# alloy v1.21.2, prometheus v3.15.1, redis_exporter v1.95.0 — all now scan
# clean); these two are what remains. Exposure: both bind
# ${AGENT_BIND_IP:-127.0.0.1} only and are reached over the internal compose
# network. Reaching this bug needs the process to be a TLS *client* to a peer
# an attacker can intercept AND that peer to present a chain through a
# distrusted intermediate. Grafana's provisioned data sources are plain
# http://prometheus:9090 and http://loki:3100, and Alertmanager's receivers
# are a local logger webhook plus Slack/PagerDuty/email entries whose
# endpoints are placeholders in this repository — so the egress path is not
# active as shipped, and where an operator activates a real HTTPS receiver the
# preconditions above still have to be met. Not claimed: that neither process
# ever speaks TLS outbound (Grafana's own update/analytics calls are TLS);
# claimed: the exploit path needs an interception position we do not concede,
# and the fix is the publisher's to ship.
#
# Carriers:
#   - grafana/grafana:13.2.4-ubuntu
#   - prom/alertmanager:v0.34.1
# Reachability: internal-monitoring-only
# Severity: HIGH
# Re-check when: grafana/grafana or prom/alertmanager publish a tag rebuilt
# with Go >= 1.26.10
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2027-01-21

